  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When benzyl bromide is treated with AgCN, it forms&nbsp;benzyl isocyanide. This reaction is followed by the S<sub>N</sub><sup>2</sup>&nbsp;mechanism.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d5e448ea-9e15-4dba-a353-eabd991eb661-9895856_S1.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 158px;\" /></p><p>Benzylamine on heating with chloroform and ethanolic potassium hydroxide forms Benzyl&nbsp;isocyanides. &nbsp;This reaction is known as carbylamine reaction or isocyanide test.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/fee9d791-3ca2-4fbf-b158-da374bcaec68-9895856_S2.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 153px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;amine does not give carbylamine&nbsp;reaction.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/0ed45165-0191-4cb6-b96f-0fae0159394d-336c83ed-8337-4c88-8a0e-11abd6d0f403-9895856_S3.png\" style=\"width: 559px; height: 117px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1ddd6e5b-bbc2-43c3-bbc5-18165898d165-9895856_S4.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 124px;\" />&nbsp;So, the correct option is C.</p>",
